https://leetcode.com/problems/linked-list-cycle-ii/description/

public class Solution {
    public ListNode detectCycle(ListNode head) {
        if (head == null || head.next == null) return null;

        ListNode slow = head;
        ListNode fast = head;

        // Step 1: Detect cycle
        while (fast != null && fast.next != null) {
            slow = slow.next;
            fast = fast.next.next;

            if (slow == fast) {
                // Step 2: Find cycle start
                ListNode ptr1 = head;
                ListNode ptr2 = slow;
                while (ptr1 != ptr2) {
                    ptr1 = ptr1.next;
                    ptr2 = ptr2.next;
                }
                return ptr1; // cycle start
            }
        }
        return null; // no cycle
    }
}


Context
After slow and fast pointers meet inside the cycle, we know:
Distance from head to cycle start = a
Distance from cycle start to meeting point = b
Cycle length = c
Mathematically, when slow and fast meet:
Slow has traveled a + b
Fast has traveled a + b + n·c (some multiple of the cycle length)
Because fast moves twice as fast, we get:
2(a+b)=a+b+n⋅c⇒a=n⋅c−b
This means: if one pointer starts at head and the other starts at the meeting point, and both move one step at a time, they will meet at the cycle start after exactly a steps.

